    "media:imagetext": "MOHAWK-1945\nMOHAWK-1965\nMOHAWK TODAY!\nIn 1945 MOHAWK Airlines (then Robinson) was housed in temporary quarters near Ithaca, New York.\nPassengers were flown in the 3 place FAIRCHILD F-24. In April of this year, MOHAWK announced\nthe purchase of a fifth 65 passenger BAC One-Eleven Fan-jet, for service in early 1965. On May 1st,\nMOHAWK will occupy its new Executive Office building at Oneida County Airport, Utica, New York.\nMOHAWK Airlines is now the largest of U.S. regional carriers.\nMIES\nCircle No. 62 on Reader Service Card.\nMAY, 1964\n31",
